\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Prediction-fit and weighted-similarity metrics rank on hard benchmarks and die or invert on saturated ones; raw overlap does not rank at all (its hard-benchmark inversion is a verbosity confound: controlling output length moves $-0.49$ to $-0.07$). No comparison metric grades against human soundness; both verification signals do. Human columns are Pearson $r$ with bootstrap 95\% CIs on the 60-item set; gold-token logprob uses the $n{=}42$ subset with logprob available.}}{8}{table.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
